      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will not be able to implement crypto.Signer in future without breaking compatibility because here is already has a method called Sign but the signature is different from what crypto.Signer needs.  Also, crypto.Signer.Sign signs a digest, whereas here it signs the message.\n(I don\u0027t claim to know why crypto.Signer doesn\u0027t apply the digest internally but instead expects the caller to do so - any idea?)\nWould it make sense to call this method SignMessage instead of just \"Sign\" to avoid the clash?  (it\u0027s a shame crypto.Signer didn\u0027t call its method SignDigest, perhaps)",
