      "writtenOn": "2016-04-24T17:00:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This does implement crypto.Signer[1] and the test should ensure that.\n\ncrypto.Signer takes a digest and not a message because it\u0027s fairly common to hash a large amount of data for signing. That data might not be in one, convenient buffer so being able to pass the hash can be a significant optimisation.\n\nEd25519 does take the whole message, which is why opts needs to be set to zero, so indicate that no hashing has taken place. Once the CFRG signatures document[2] is ready then implementing HashEdDSA via this interface should be easy.\n\n[1] https://godoc.org/crypto#Signer\n[2] https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-irtf-cfrg-eddsa-05#section-4",
      "parentUuid": "a87f884b_27c97e98",
